      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(providers): release stream reader lock after classifying SDK stream body",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`src/agents/provider-transport-fetch.ts` calls `reader.cancel()` in the finally block of `classifyOpenAISdkStreamBody` but does not call `reader.releaseLock()`. Per the Streams specification, `reader.cancel()` rejects pending reads but does NOT release the lock — `releaseLock()` is required to allow other consumers to acquire the cloned stream.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `src/agents/provider-transport-fetch.ts`: add `try { reader.releaseLock(); } catch {}` after `reader.cancel()` in the finally block of `classifyOpenAISdkStreamBody()`\n- `src/agents/provider-transport-fetch.test.ts`: 2 vitest tests proving:\n  1. `cancel()` + `releaseLock()` properly unlocks the stream (positive control)\n  2. `cancel()` alone leaves the stream locked (negative control)\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Vitest — stream reader lock lifecycle\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run src/agents/provider-transport-fetch.test.ts\n\n ✓ stream reader lock lifecycle > requires releaseLock() after cancel() to unlock the stream\n ✓ stream reader lock lifecycle > cancel() alone leaves stream locked (negative control)\n```\n\nBefore: `reader.cancel()` → stream remains locked → other consumers blocked\nAfter: `reader.cancel()` + `reader.releaseLock()` → stream properly unlocked\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted",
        "branch": "fix/provider-classify-stream-reader-release",
        "head_sha": "6f923aaf07a09acd3d0f88d4ecb87fa444e04084",
